    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8916\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the criminal procedure law, in\nrelation to security services in the courts\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nProvides peace officer status to court security deputies, employed by\nthe Monroe County Sheriff's Department, at Monroe County court facili-\nties.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Subdivision 21 of section 2.10 of the criminal procedure law\nis amended by adding a new paragraph g to allow a deputy sheriff who is\nemployed by the sheriff's department of Monroe county to perform the\ndelivery of security services to the courts.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York State Office of Court Administration (OCA) contracts and\npays for court security personnel in the Hall of Justice, Rochester, New\nYork. OCA requires that all such personnel be certified and registered\nwith the Bureau of Municipal Police. OCA has recommended Monroe County\nto seek special legislation to allow county sheriff deputies to perform\ncourt security services.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2013-2014: S.4892a/A.3765a - passed both houses\n2011-2012: S.5454/A.720 - passed senate\n2009-2010: S.4195/A.2278\n2007-2008: S.548/A.779\n2005-2006: S.1271a/A.364a\n2003-2004: S.3525/A.1048 - passed assembly\n2001-2002: S.4521/A.99a - passed assembly\n2000: S.7156a/A.10928a - passed senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect 30 days after it shall have become a law.\n",
